# Shared homelab public ingress: Caddy on a public-IP VM (Oracle Cloud Always Free),
# reachable from the internet and reverse-proxying to homelab services over Tailscale.
# The home network is double-NAT with no usable port-forward, so this edge is how
# anything gets exposed publicly. Certs are Let's Encrypt via the HTTP-01 challenge
# (the box has a public IP and open port 80), so no DNS-provider token is needed here.
#
# Add an app with a block: <public-host> { reverse_proxy <tailnet-ip>:<port> }.
# Only expose what should be public; admin UIs stay tailnet-only.

jellyfin.majed.fyi {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 100.84.50.127:8096
}

jellyseerr.majed.fyi {
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 100.84.50.127:5055
}
